course: dictionary
lesson: 14424
title: Big words, big meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Oversized is made of two parts: over and size. You can see the word size inside it, and the start over- suggests more than usual. So oversized means bigger than the normal size. «Mia wore an oversized jumper that reached down to her knees.» A jumper is usually a normal size, so oversized tells you hers was much too big. Try the swap: «Mia wore a very big jumper» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Oversized can also mean too big for its purpose. «The toddler's hat was oversized and kept slipping over his eyes.» A hat that is too big for its job does not fit, so it is oversized. The clue is the words kept slipping over his eyes, which show the hat is too big for the head it is on.
explain: Look at what the word describes. Oversized clothes are often made big on purpose, as a fashion style. Oversized luggage is just too large for its job, like a bag that will not fit in the car. Always check the words around oversized first, because they tell you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Oversized means bigger than the normal size; very large.
fact: Oversized can also mean too big for its purpose, like an oversized coat on a small child.
fact: Oversized is an adjective: it describes a noun, such as «oversized jumper» or «oversized luggage».
fact: In fashion, oversized clothes are made big on purpose.
fact: Oversized means about the same as very big, so you can use it in place of «very big» in a sentence.
exercise: «The giant oversized sandwich was too big for one person.» What does oversized mean here? | Cut into small pieces | Made of cheese | *Very large | Eaten quickly
exercise: Ella's boots were oversized, so she clumped along like a clown. What does oversized mean? | *Much too big for her feet | Made of wood | Shiny and new | Very quiet
exercise: Which word means the opposite of oversized? | Massive | Enormous | *Tiny | Wide
test: «The oversized bag was too heavy for the little girl to carry.» What does oversized suggest? | Light and soft | *Too big for the little girl | Brand new
test: Why might a shop sell oversized jumpers on purpose? | Because jumpers are always too small | Because they are the cheapest to make | *Because some people like loose, big clothes in fashion
exam: Which sentence uses oversized correctly? | Oversized means very small and neat. | The oversized tent was a tiny pebble on the table. | *The oversized tent could fit twelve people inside.
